  "notes": "A patch release for the window, prompted by a user report that it could not be moved.\n\n## Fixed\n- **Windows: the window can be moved.** Drag it by the empty part of the title bar, the logo or the empty space in the sidebar; double-click there to maximise. gpui's window-move call does nothing on Windows, so the window now marks those areas as its caption instead.\n- **macOS: the window resizes from its edges.** A gpui window without a system title bar wasn't resizable. The greyed-out traffic lights over the sidebar are gone as well; Skidbladnir draws its own window buttons.\n- **macOS: the window buttons respond at once.** The top 28px was a native drag strip, and AppKit held back clicks there while it checked for a double-click. The app now handles that strip itself.\n\nInstallers for Windows, macOS (Apple Silicon and Intel) and Linux are attached by the release workflow; existing installs update themselves.\n\nNote: merged before PR CI finished on Windows and macOS (#80); the release workflow's builds are the first full builds of this code on those platforms."
}
